description:
**Experience 10 to 15years**

**Hospital Experience Prefered**

Maintenance Incharge ( Engineer)

Duties may include but are not limited to the following:

* Monitors, repairs, installs, and adjusts all types of specialized hospital equipment and systems, such as oxygen systems, vacuum systems, medical gases and related systems, projectors, fire life safety systems, lights and other types of medical systems and equipment gases and related systems, projectors, fire life safety systems, lights and other types of medical systems and equipment;
* Services air conditioning, refrigeration, dishwashers, air compressors, fans, pumps, motors, garbage disposals, heating and ventilation systems and devices, and steam heat exchangers;
* Receives preventive maintenance work orders and performs hospital rounds according to schedule to identify and make repairs to systems;
* Makes minor plumbing and electrical connections on equipment installation or repairs; may perform appliance equipment repairs as needed;
* Performs minor repairs on buildings such as screens, windows, floors, ceilings, walls, roofs, doors, cabinets, and tile;
* Paints equipment rooms as necessary;
* Completes and submits work records; records status of equipment, readings, hours of operation, fuel consumed, temperature or pressure, water levels and voltage load, etc.;
* Operates and drives light trucks and operates motorized equipment;
* Keeps facilities clean in appearance; and
* Performs other related duties as required.

Typical Qualifications

These are entrance requirements to the exam process and assure neither continuance in the process nor placement on an eligible list.

**EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE and TRAINING**

Any combination of education and experience which has led to the acquisition of the required knowledge, skills and abilities, which can be demonstrated by the following:

Four (4) years of combined experience in the application of the following trades: plumbing, electrical, HVAC, carpentry, painting and alarm systems, **OR**

Four (4) years of experience in any of the following trades: plumbing, electrical, HVAC, carpentry, painting and alarm systems.

**NECESSARY SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS**

* Possession and maintenance of a valid California driver license is required for the operation of equipment normally assigned to this classification.
* Incumbent must be able to sit, stand, walk, kneel crouch, squat, stoop, reach, twist and lift heavy objects.
* Must be willing and able to occasionally work evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed.

**DESIRED**

One (1) year of experience as a building mechanic in a hospital setting is highly desirable.

**Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:**

Comprehensive knowledge of:

* applicable State, County and City codes relevant to the installation, operation and repair of electrical and mechanical equipment;
* the methods and means of repairing a wide variety of electrical, mechanical, plumbing, and specialized hospital equipment;
* tools and materials used in the repair of mechanical and electrical equipment
* hospital systems and related equipment;
* applicable preventive maintenance schedules and techniques;
* occupational hazards and safety precautions;
* on-line work order applications.

Job Type: Permanent

Pay: Up to ₹55,000.00 per month

Benefits:

* Provident Fund

Work Location: In person
